From 89e655f62e02733b511481aa87be5f4fbf4eee2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:58:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0234 diagnostic: B-cut probe for S/T/slot fields and grow
 V/arena bump/end

The Explorer/Football/Mechanic abort is a deliberate SDK abort in the
grow branch of allocator 0x954310 (REPORT-GROW-ROOTCAUSE.md): the arena
bumps past its end while loading a SARC archive, so it calls the heap's
grow virtual function V, which aborts. Static disassembly pinned the
container (a shared SARC-loading arena), the grow sizes (925,888 /
946,368 / 430,272), and count Path B (4096), but four values are
runtime-only and cannot be pinned statically: S and T (the two virtual
returns in B that feed size and count), [x28,#0x30] (the size source,
whose write point was not found), V (the heap grow virtual function),
and the arena's bump/end at the abort instant.

Two additions, both logging-only and both reusing the 0230/0232 grow
ring (magic "GRWR", drained once per present and once more from the SVC
Break handler on the abort, so the aborting records survive):
- A B cut at 0x97e114 (`ldp w9, w8, [x28, #0x30]`, right after S (w26)
  and T (w0) are computed) records S, T, [x28,#0x30], [x28,#0x24],
  [x28,#0x34], [x28,#0x20] into the grow ring, write-time filtered to
  [x28,#0x30] > 256KB (the aborting sizes are 430,272+, most B calls are
  small) so the ring is not overwhelmed.
- The grow body now also records V ([[heap_iface]], vtable slot 0), the
  heap interface pointer ([x25,#0x10]), and the arena bump/end
  ([container,#0xe0] / [container,#0xe8]) at the grow cut, so the log
  shows V's identity and the remaining space (end - bump) at the abort.
The grow record grows 64 -> 96 bytes and the ring shrinks 16 -> 8
records (the state page still fits with room to spare); the drain logs
B records and grow records with their own field names, told apart by
site. Temporary: remove the cuts and the drain once the abort trigger
is pinned. This build only gathers data; it does not fix the abort.
